  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: b30d5d35fb2e3104b900a6c4d6d96e99, type: 3}
  m_Name: MathQuestion
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  questionStatement: Which is not a Newton's Law
  options:
  - A body remains at rest, or in motion at a constant speed in a straight line,
    unless it is acted upon by a force.
  - At any instant of time, the net force on a body is equal to the body's acceleration
    multiplied by its mass
  - What goes around comes around
  - To every action, there is always opposed an equal reaction
  correctAnswerIndex: 2
